        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "162bb71f-5f07-5196-b729-11b4680091aa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Al-Ghazali, Ibn Rushd\n- Roles: theologian, jurist, philosopher, mystic, polymath\n- Places: Persia, al-Andalus, Western medieval world\n\nFacts:\n- Al-Ghazali, born in 1058 and died on 19 December 1111, was Abū Ḥāmid Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Ghazālī.\n- Al-Ghazali was shortened as Al-Ghazali in Arabic and Ghazali in Persian, and he was known as Algazelus or Algazel in the Western medieval world.\n- Al-Ghazali was a Persian theologian, jurist, philosopher, and mystic.\n- Ibn Rushd, born on 14 April 1126 and died on 10 December 1198, was a medieval Andalusian polymath.\n- Ibn Rushd was often Latinized as Averroes.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
